    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19323" root="سدس" body-key="s">
    
      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سدّسهُ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَسْدِيسٌ</span>, <i>He made it six.</i> (EshSheybánee, and K voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَحَّدَهُ</span>.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <i>He made it to
be six-cornered; six-angled; hexagonal:</i> or <i>sixribbed.</i> (Sgh, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سدّس لِٱمْرَأَتِهِ</span>, or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عِنْدَهَا</span>,
<i>He remained six nights with his wife:</i> and in like
manner the verb is used in relation to any saying
or action. (TA voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَبَّعَ</span>.)

